export anchor WitchHourStyle:
    number: 317
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Witch hour
    idea: A deep purple night watch where services stand as potion bottles on a shelf filled to their uptime, charts sit in arched windows under a thin moon, and green glows only where things are well.
    base: dark
    palette:
        midnight: #150c21, the page under a faint violet glow at top right
        robe: #20132e, arched windows, cards, bottle tags and the style sheet
        robeRaised: #2a1a3c, the incident card, the current tab and list rows
        ink: #f4edff, text
        mist: #c2b3da, captions, times and axis
        line: #4b3668, borders, rules and the log thread
        shelf: #3a2752, the shelf plank under the bottles
        potionGreen: #7cf0a8, healthy potion, the glowing request line, p50, the primary button, focus, Healthy and Resolved
        violet: #c7a2ff, the moon mark, stars, p95, log beads and the secondary button border
        amber: #ffcb6b, degraded potion, Degraded and Investigating with triangle and magnifier
        moonblue: #8fd3ff, recovered potion, Recovered with a diamond
        rose: #ff94a7, Firing with an octagon, the error line
    type:
        Headings in Palatino Linotype, Book Antiqua, Palatino, Georgia at
        600, body in Gill Sans, Segoe UI, Calibri. Base 16px at 1.5. The
        incident ID is 30px serif, the brand 26px serif with an italic 15px
        subtitle, section titles 21px serif, uptime figures 22px serif with
        old style numbers, captions 14 to 15px italic serif.
    layout:
        A centred 1120px column. The header holds a violet crescent moon
        with a small green star, Brightwork Ops with the italic line The
        night watch over production, last 24 hours, and the suite apps with
        a green underline on Ops. The first section, The shelf of services,
        shows five flask bottles standing on a purple plank. Each flask is
        filled to its uptime on a 99 to 100 percent scale, green for
        healthy, amber for degraded with bubbles, pale blue for recovered
        with a small crack. A string hangs from each bottle to a tag card
        with the service name, status shape and word, the figure and one
        fact. A caption says how the fill is read and that billing shows its
        outage. Next, two columns. The left is an arched window with stars
        and a moon holding Requests per minute as a glowing green area
        chart with an italic 9,400 note. The right holds the incident card
        with a double rule, INC-0427, its facts and two pill buttons, then
        The night log, a thread of alerts with violet beads. Last, three
        small arched windows for Error rate, Latency and Fresh brews, the
        deploys. Below 900px columns stack, below 760px bottles sit left of
        their tags in rows with a plank under each.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters and gaps, 22px card padding, bottles on a 16px grid.
    density: Airy. Five bottles across, one big arched chart, then three small arches.
    corners: Arched tops on chart windows using 260 by 120px elliptical corners with 12px at the foot. 12px cards, 20px pill buttons, 10px fields.
    borders: 1px violet grey lines. The incident card has a double rule made by an inset outline.
    shadows: No drop shadows. The request line glows green and the shelf has a hard 6px dark edge below it.
    icons:
        Flask bottles filled to uptime and a crescent moon mark. Status
        pairs the word with a filled circle, triangle, diamond, octagon,
        square or a magnifier.
    focus: A 2px potion green outline offset 3px with a soft green halo.
    tone: Lightly storybook headings such as The shelf of services, The night log and Fresh brews, with plain facts underneath.
